  "Question": "If \\(64\\) is divided into three parts proportional to \\(2,\\) \\(4,\\) and \\(6,\\) the smallest part is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(5\\dfrac{1}{3}\\)",
    "B": "\\(11\\)",
    "C": "\\(10\\dfrac{2}{3}\\)",
    "D": "\\(5\\)",
    "E": "None of these answers"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The ratio \\(2:4:6\\) means that the three parts contain \\(2\\), \\(4\\), and \\(6\\) equal-sized shares. There are \\(2+4+6=12\\) shares altogether, and the smallest part contains \\(2\\) of them. Therefore the smallest part is\n\\[\n\\frac{64}{12}\\cdot 2=\\frac{32}{3}=10\\frac{2}{3}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{10\\frac{2}{3}}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
